-- chem/electric.cub — Thiemann's electric operator at a vertex, exactly, and the electric energy of a U(1)
-- charge network there. QSD V eq. 3.8 sums over pairs of edges e, e′ at v the operator
--   O_ee′ = tr[h_e[h_e⁻¹, √V] h_e′[h_e′⁻¹, √V]] = 2V − √V tr M_e′ − tr M_e √V + tr(M_e M_e′),   M_e = h_e √V h_e⁻¹,
-- times X_e X_e′, which on a charge network with integer labels n_e is n_e n_e′. tr M_e is chem/rootsum.cub's
-- edge-trace. tr(M_e M_e′) is read off the order of the indices: M_e′ attaches a line to e′ (E, leg a′ open),
-- √V acts, and closing it on e′ emits a leg b′ (F̃); M_e attaches a line to e whose leg is contracted with b′
-- (E, then the ε contraction), √V acts, and closing e takes up a′ (R). Each line's far end is contracted before
-- the next line is attached, so the weights are the single-edge ones, (2j′+1)/(2j_e′+1) and (2j″+1)/(2j_e+1).
-- F̃ is fixed by contracting its emitted leg with the open one giving R: from the spin-(j+½) side F̃ = (d′/(d′+1))E₋,
-- from the spin-(j−½) side F̃ = −E₊ (d′ the attached edge's doubled spin); the factors √s that make the Bargmann
-- maps isometric cancel between each attaching and closing, so every coefficient is rational. With √V = M^{1/8}/√2
-- and V = M^{1/4}/2 (M = 16 Q_v², chem/rootsum.cub), every term is a weight times
--   Σ_{m₁(x)=0} Σ_{m₂(y)=0} x^{a/8} y^{b/8} Σ_{p,q} x^p y^q D_pq / (m₁′(x) m₂′(y)),
-- with m₁, m₂ rational polynomials and D_pq rational matrices on the vertex's states.
import "rootsum.hypercubical"

